          'Printed-role Karama stopping a clean native CHOAM revival benefit, Tleilaxu granted force limit or discount, early leader revival or Advanced foreign Ghola also offers its exact used cost. The original request stays unpaid and its counters or leader stay in the Tanks through the offer. Claim or Continue finishes the original prevention once: native rules may abandon the request, reprice it, open its remaining response or complete an affordable return. Unfunded repricing returns nothing and consumes no allowance. Any income follows the actual return once; taking Karama cannot repeat the request. Other unfinished parents remain separate.',
          'Printed-role Karama stopping native Fremen Storm protection, worm survival, allied worm protection or Advanced additional-worm placement offers its exact used cost before prevention. Claim or Continue finishes that cancellation once. Storm entry keeps its already-deposited cohort and queued arrival through the offer; denial then kills that original group without shipping again. Storm traversal, devouring, later survival responses, Spice draws and rides remain native. A summoned worm retains its own saved parent until native completion. Other unfinished parents retain their separate boundaries.',
          'Printed-role Karama stopping native Voice, ordinary Prescience, Kwisatz Haderach, elite strength, Fremen support or CHOAM battle aid offers its exact used cost while the original battle waits. Claim or Continue finishes that prevention once, then native preparation or the next power check resumes. The offer does not answer Prescience, seal or reveal plans, charge support, spend a reserved pledge or change the forces. Taking Karama does not restore the canceled benefit. The separate live Nexus borrowed-Voice parent retains its existing cancellation path; wider combinations remain unfinished.',
          'Karama stopping Harkonnen’s extra card after a purchase, a Richese No-Field declaration or Harkonnen’s Traitor call for an ally also offers its used cost. Claim or Continue keeps the original purchase paid and prevents only the bonus draw. A denied No-Field moves no token or forces and charges no shipment; the original ordinary shipment or independent Ambassador reserve grant remains available. An allied Traitor cancellation preserves revealed plans and earlier votes, changes only Harkonnen’s effective call, then finishes the original battle once. The physical Traitor is never a Semuta target. Supported Ambassador cases are Basic; broader combinations remain unfinished.',
